%N A212176 Row n of table lists exponents in canonical prime factorization of A181800(n) (n-th powerful number that is the first integer of its prime signature), in nonincreasing order.
%C A212176 A212179(n) gives length of row n.
%C A212176 Table represents prime signature (cf. A212171) and second signature (cf. A212172) of A181800.
%H A212176 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A212176/b212176.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..11185</a> (rows 2..3000, flattened)
%H A212176 Will Nicholes, <a href="https://willnicholes.com/2010/06/06/prime-signatures">Prime signatures</a>.
%F A212176 Row n is identical to row A181800(n) of tables A212171 and A212172.
%e A212176 Table begins:
%e A212176   2
%e A212176   3
%e A212176   4
