%e A212176 Since 72 is a member of A181800, all positive exponents in its prime factorization (2^3*3^2) equal or exceed 2. Therefore, its second signature is the same as its prime signature, namely, {3,2} (nonincreasing version).  Since 72 = A181800 (8), row 8 represents the prime signature and second signature {3,2}.
%t A212176 v = Import["https://oeis.org/A181800/b181800.txt", "Table"][[;; , 2]];
%t A212176 e[n_] := FactorInteger[n][[;; , 2]];
%t A212176 e /@ v[[2 ;; 47]] // Flatten (* _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 22 2026 *)
%Y A212176 Cf. A181800, A212171, A212172, A212179.
